causes={
 '1_front_joins':'Fit1 pinned measured curve positions/depths and solved separate harmonic interiors without slope coupling. Full relief creases terminated at the outline; the independently resampled rim stood only about 0.4 mm from several tips. Its local depth differences and outline-depth/control-spacing variation concentrated curvature at those C0 joins. Camera rays, editable crease overlays and exported join profiles locate these in the fitted surface, rather than only the low bake.',
 '2_low_notch':'The low reducer protected field projection but not the whole front and permitted very slender faces. At the reported notch, the original maximum aspect ratio was 1157.03; several detached atlas triangles had only 2-7 texels of area. The 338.93-degree audit found errors up to 22.35 degrees while actual bake-ray and nearest-high reference normals agreed to about 0.002 degrees at the worst sample. This implicates UV/reduction support, not a wrong-surface ray at that notch.',
 '3_rear_and_normals':'The original rear relaxation retained a 0.015 attraction to every original sparse depth, leaving lower-rear bumps. Original side-classified normal errors also included steep star walls: the worst nearest-reference error was 101.52 degrees, with both tiny-chart bake error and reference ambiguity at split normals (nearest versus ray reached 92.18 degrees). Zero sampled ray misses did not certify those texels.',
 '4_suspension':'The generated bar cage comprised three disconnected rails: duplicate front/back left rails and a rear right rail, separated by internal cuts around the loop. Fit1 retained all of them and the original bulky loop section. The fitted sparse body boundary also left a small lower-neck gap detected by surface-distance checks.'}
fixes={
 'front':'Retain every original X/Z feature control and independent generated sector. Smooth only measured curve depths; terminate relief creases gradually before the outline and taper their central starts. Match each terminal branch depth derivative to the surrounding measured boundary neighbourhood with a Hermite continuation. A shared sparse minimum-bending solve couples field/rim slopes. The 0.65 semi-sharp outline and softened rim supports have C1 subdivision-limit continuity instead of hard split normal fans at those joins.',
 'low_and_uv':'All front and rear collapse candidates preserve projected orientation; field and surface-region boundaries remain immutable even where they have zero geometric crease. The reducer rejects worsening slender triangles above aspect 60. The front and rear receive continuous charts initialized from X/Z; all body charts receive intrinsic minimum-stretch relaxation so steep walls have sufficient texel area. No UV island edge crosses a front notch. Hardware retains the established chart method. Padding is 0.008.',
 'rear':'Eight implicit sparse diffusion steps of 16 mm2 each heavily low-pass the generated rear depth, followed by boundary-constrained minimum bending with 0.001 weak fidelity to that filtered prior. The rim-edge boundary remains the source; raw-depth attraction is removed. No dense raw projection or ideal plate is introduced.',
 'hardware':hardware}
